====================================================================================================
PART C: crossover(n,gamma)'s limit = D(gamma)+1-1/(2*gamma) is
        LOGICALLY EQUIVALENT to C(gamma) itself (elementary algebra)
====================================================================================================
IF C(gamma) holds (S_n'=1+G_n+D(gamma)+o(1)), THEN crossover(n,gamma) -> D_gamma + 1 - 1/(2*gamma)
Predecessor's cited conjectural target: D(gamma)+1-1/(2*gamma)
Difference (should be 0): 0

CONFIRMED (elementary algebra, exact): crossover(n,gamma) -> 
D(gamma)+1-1/(2*gamma) is not an INDEPENDENT fact still to be found by
more matched-asymptotics work -- it is, by the PROVED exact
decomposition above, LOGICALLY EQUIVALENT to C(gamma) itself (S_n=
G_n+D(gamma)+o(1)) holding. Any argument that rigorously computed
crossover(n,gamma)'s closed-form limit and confirmed it equals the
cited target would, by this same equivalence, CONSTITUTE a proof of
C(gamma) -- clearly outside a single front's scope, and exactly why
a 'local' inner/outer matching argument (script 04), which only
certifies CONSISTENCY of two asymptotic pictures in their common
region of validity, cannot by itself resolve it. See ATTEMPT.md
Section 6 for the full discussion.
